# AI Tools — Second Brain for Developers

Three ready-to-use tools that connect your local models to your daily workflow.

## 1. Editor AI — Autocomplete + Chat in VS Code / JetBrains

Continue.dev extension configured to use your local Ollama models.
Works with **VS Code**, **WebStorm**, **PhpStorm**, **IntelliJ IDEA**, and all other JetBrains IDEs.
- Inline autocomplete as you type (Tab to accept)
- Chat panel for questions, refactoring, explanations (Ctrl+L / Alt+Shift+J)
- Edit selected code in place (Ctrl+I)
- Semantic codebase search (@Codebase)

Model: qwen3-coder-30b-editor (autocomplete) + qwen3-coder-30b-safe (chat)
Config: .continue/config.json
Guide:  docs/editor-ai.md

## 2. Agent AI — Multi-Step Task Automation

Python script that breaks a high-level task into a numbered plan, then
executes each step with full context — like a project manager in your terminal.

    python3 scripts/agent.py "add input validation to the Express API"
    python3 scripts/agent.py "write tests for the auth module"
    python3 scripts/agent.py  # interactive mode

Model: qwen3-coder-30b-agent
Guide: docs/agent-ai.md

## 3. CLI AI — Quick Commands, Scripts & Git Help

Two bash scripts for fast AI assistance from the terminal.

    ai "write a one-liner to find all TODO comments in .ts files"
    echo "SyntaxError: unexpected token" | ai "explain this error"

    git add -A && git-ai commit   # Generate commit message
    git-ai review                 # Code review before committing
    git-ai pr main                # Draft PR description
    git-ai explain HEAD~2         # Explain a past commit

Model: qwen3-4b-cli (fast, concise, terminal-friendly)
Guide: docs/cli-ai.md

## Quick Start

    # 1. Start Docker services
    docker-compose up -d

    # 2. Set up CLI tools
    chmod +x scripts/ai.sh scripts/git-ai.sh
    sudo ln -sf "$(pwd)/scripts/ai.sh"     /usr/local/bin/ai
    sudo ln -sf "$(pwd)/scripts/git-ai.sh" /usr/local/bin/git-ai

    # 3. Set up your editor (choose one)

    # VS Code
    code --install-extension continue.continue

    # JetBrains (WebStorm, PhpStorm, IntelliJ IDEA, etc.)
    # Install "Continue" from JetBrains Marketplace (Settings → Plugins → Marketplace)

    # Copy the config (same for all IDEs)
    cp .continue/config.json ~/.continue/config.json

    # 4. Try it
    ai "hello, are you there?"
    git-ai log
